            <name>Commercial roof search (blue) — new/updated today</name>
            <Placemark id="17">
                <name>Johnston CSD - Johnston Middle School (+ Wallace Elementary alternates) (Johnston, IA)</name>
                <description>seeking roofer (public bid) - MATERIAL UPDATE | 2026-10-16 (notice published); mandatory pre-bid Wed 2026-10-28 1:00 PM; bids due 2026-11-12 3:00 PM; board award 11/23
UPDATE to a lead first listed 10/17 (that listing only said "due Nov 12"). Full notice now posted: Johnston Middle School Partial Re-Roof Phase III, base bid tears off ballasted/adhered EPDM and installs 2" polyiso + 1/2" HD cover board + fully adhered 60-mil EPDM on ~70,000 SF, plus ~10,000 SF vertical metal siding; 2 alternates re-roof ~35,000 SF at Wallace Elementary (~1,000 ft east). MANDATORY pre-bid Oct 28 1:00 PM at JCSD Middle School, 6501 NW 62nd Ave (bidders who miss it cannot bid unless they arrange a walk-through with the owner before 10/28). 5% bid security. Plans from Beeline &amp; Blue, Des Moines ($50 refundable deposit).
Contact: Mark Thiessen, Angelo Architectural Associates (architect); owner rep Rick Stark, Director of Buildings &amp; Grounds (phone redacted on notice) · 515-250-6950 (architect, from 10/17 plan-room brief)
Website: 
Confidence: confirmed (official notice text)
Source: https://www.noticeregistry.com/iowa/notice/bid-notice-johnston-132159
~119 mi from Omaha | preferred state: Yes</description>
                <styleUrl>#18</styleUrl>
                <Point id="16">
                    <coordinates>-93.6977,41.673,0.0</coordinates>
                </Point>
            </Placemark>
            <Placemark id="22">
                <name>Kansas State University - Waters Hall (Manhattan, KS)</name>
                <description>seeking roofer (state capital project - design stage) | 2026-10-15 (advertised in Kansas Register #54623); SBAC nomination slated for the Nov 18, 2026 meeting
New capital improvement ad: "KSU Waters Hall ReRoof - #54623 - October 15, 2026" for architectural/engineering services; listed for State Building Advisory Commission nominations on Nov 18, 2026. Design-phase now, so the roofing construction bid should follow after the architect is selected (early relationship target with the A/E). Roof size/system not stated on the page; the Kansas Register ad text did not load in a read-only fetch.
Contact: KS DoA OFPM professional qualifications inbox (A/E submittals) · professional.qualifications@ks.gov
Website: https://admin.ks.gov
Confidence: confirmed listing; scope/size unconfirmed (map pin at K-State campus, approximate)
Source: https://admin.ks.gov/offices/facilities-property-management/design-construction--compliance/architectural--engineering-advertisements-nominations-and-selections
~147 mi from Omaha | preferred state: Yes</description>
